<%# The household-library hub. Everything here is a thing you already own
    and currently keep somewhere worse. %>

<section class="mt-12 max-w-3xl space-y-5">
  <p>
    Most of what matters to a household is already in files: the lease, the
    insurance policy, twelve years of photographs, the recipe your
    grandmother wrote out, the password to the account nobody can get into
    since the funeral. It lives across four services, three of which could
    change their terms next year, and one shoebox.
  </p>
  <p>
    This is where it lives instead — on a disk you can hold.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="mt-14">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">What it holds</h2>
  <div class="mt-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Documents") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Files, with their text pulled out so you can search inside them, and
        a plain-language summary of what each one actually says. The point of
        filing the lease is being able to answer a question about the lease.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Photos and albums") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        The family library, on your own storage. Albums you can share with
        the household, or hand to one relative by a link that needs no
        account.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Recipes") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A recipe box that understands ingredients well enough to scale a
        batch, gathered into books, and shareable outside the house in a
        format another copy of this app can simply import.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Email") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        Your mail, mirrored down onto your own disk from your own provider,
        so the app can notice the bill and the deadline in it without any of
        it passing through anyone else.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "Passwords") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A vault, encrypted with a key derived from your passphrase, with
        one-time codes and sharing to the people who will one day need in.
      </p>
    <% end %>
    <%= render Ui::CardComponent.new(title: "A diary") do %>
      <p class="text-sm text-soft">
        A second sealed container, where everything but the date is
        encrypted. Nobody with the database file can read it. Neither can the
        rest of the app.
      </p>
    <% end %>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="mt-14 max-w-3xl">
  <h2 class="display text-2xl">Private means private from the house, too</h2>
  <p class="mt-4 text-soft">
    Everything here starts visible to you alone — not merely hidden from the
    internet, but hidden from the other people signed in to the same
    installation. Sharing is per item or per area, always something you
    switched on, and always listed where you can see and revoke it. Two
    things go further and stay sealed even from someone with the machine:
    the password vault and the diary.
  </p>
  <p class="mt-5">
    <%= link_to "How the privacy model works →", about_page_path("privacy"), class: "text-primary-700 hover:underline" %>
  </p>
</section>
